Build (uses your system ROCm install; see patches/README.md for the full env-knob list):
  cmake -B build -DGGML_HIP=ON -DGGML_HIP_RCCL=1 -DGPU_TARGETS="gfx1100;gfx1151;gfx1201" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
  cmake --build build -j

  GPU_TARGETS is read from the environment if set; the default builds for all three
  RDNA families the set supports (one binary runs on any of them; trim to your GPU
  for a faster build):
    gfx1100  RDNA 3   (RX 7900 XTX/XT, RX 7800 XT, ...)
    gfx1151  RDNA 3.5 (Strix Point / Strix Halo APUs)
    gfx1201  RDNA 4   (RX 9070 XT / 9070; gfx1200 = RX 9060 XT)
  All three compile with ROCm >= 6.3 (RDNA4 codegen officially from 6.4.x; this set
  was verified on ROCm 7.14).  Keep GGML_HIP_RCCL=1: block 12's hybrid all-reduce
  uses RCCL for the large-tensor path, and on non-RDNA4 (gfx1100/gfx1151) the
  internal AR is gated off and everything falls back to RCCL.
  Optional (both ON by default upstream; keep for parity with the tuned reference build):
    -DGGML_HIP_GRAPHS=ON -DGGML_NATIVE=1

